     "titulo": "Long vowel and double consonant",
     "texto": [
      "In many pairs, a vowel before a double consonant is usually short; before a single consonant it can be long. Compare **tak–takk** and **mate–matte** with a reliable recording. Tonal accent and exact realisation vary by dialect; spelling alone does not let you verify the exact sound."
